<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109636" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπ-όψιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑφοράω,</span>
		fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπόψομαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>viewed from beneath</i> the brows, i.e. <i>viewed
				with suspicious looks,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λώβην τ᾽ ἔμεναι καὶ ὑπόψιον ἄλλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.42
				</span></i>
			 (where, however, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.Byz.
			</span></i> read <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπόψιον,</span>
			
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπόψιος</span>
			), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				13.289
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>under the eye</i> or <i>view, conspicuous,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				1.30
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
